{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.jet_filtered_knot_factor","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jet_filtered_knot_factor","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jet_filtered_knot_factor.factor_is_jones","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jet_filtered_knot_factor.factor_is_jones","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/jet_filtered_knot_factor.lean#L68-L68","doc":"**The conjecture** (Part 4): the BW knot factor equals the Jones\npolynomial of the nuclear quotient braid, for every $(Z, N)$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jet_filtered_knot_factor.jonesQuotient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jet_filtered_knot_factor.jonesQuotient","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/jet_filtered_knot_factor.lean#L65-L65","doc":"The Jones polynomial $J_{\\bar\\beta}(q)$ of the nuclear quotient\nbraid (each nucleon collapsed to one effective crossing). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jet_filtered_knot_factor.knotFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jet_filtered_knot_factor.knotFactor","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/jet_filtered_knot_factor.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The Bethe–Weizsäcker knot factor $a(Z, N)$ multiplying the bulk\nbinding (the $q$-Plancherel-weighted per-level invariant of Part 1,\nwith weights `jetWedderburnWeight`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jet_filtered_knot_factor.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jet_filtered_knot_factor.mk","kind":"ctor","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/jet_filtered_knot_factor.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jet_filtered_knot_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jet_filtered_knot_factor","kind":"class","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/jet_filtered_knot_factor.lean#L54-L68","doc":"**Jet-filtered knot factor** $a(Z, N) = J_{\\bar\\beta}(q)$.\n\nConjectural class — see\n[`conj:jet-filtered-knot-factor`](../../../quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jet-filtered-knot-factor.md). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:jet-filtered-knot-factor","label":"conj:jet-filtered-knot-factor","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/jet-filtered-knot-factor.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jetWedderburnWeight_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jetWedderburnWeight_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/jet_filtered_knot_factor.lean#L47-L52","doc":"The jet Wedderburn weights are non-negative — a **proved** (sorry-free)\nconsequence of $q$-Plancherel positivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jetWedderburnWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jetWedderburnWeight","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/jet_filtered_knot_factor.lean#L35-L45","doc":"The per-jet-level **Wedderburn weight** $w_\\lambda = d_q(\\lambda)^2 /\nZ_q(k)$ feeding the established per-level invariant $a_k$ (manuscript\nPart 1), realised as the canonical $q$-Plancherel measure.\n\n§7c: stated over a generic ordered field `R`; the `q`-Plancherel measure\nit wraps is itself generic (`QOU.MathlibExt.QPlancherel.measure`), so\nnothing here is archimedean. The archimedean evaluation is the\ninstantiation `R := ℝ` at the substrate. ","signatureChunk":0}]}